readme='''Round01 creature-fish BODY — native editor handoff, no approval\n\nStart with delivery.json, validation.json, native-validation.json, geometry-ledger.json and sheet-coverage.json. Heroes are exactly N/E/S/W. Required state/facing preview aliases intentionally share complete state/four-direction phase sheets; all twelve phase columns and explicit source path/hash/cell mappings are retained.\n\nEditable source: ../../source/round-01.blend, SHA256 '''+project_sha+''' . The entire required native capture was rendered after reopening that exact saved file. Every native4x1792x2048 frame is retained; published2x896x1024 frames use only uniform wholecanvas Pillow LANCZOS reduction, then exact original6x2 atlases. No crop/fit/warp/recolor/alpha/RGB repair is used for delivered frames. Explicitly labeled enlarged diagnostic crops and video overview crops are review media only.\n\nNative implementation: reconstructed continuous rounded body with cobalt/cyan vertex colors and pale underside; padded cambered tail/side/dorsal fin volumes; native ivory eye whites/ocean irises/navy pupils/pearl glints and modest turquoise mouth. Existing five-bone chain and eleven source actions retained. Bones use Euler XYZ, matching keyed Euler channels; source bone rotation curves scaled0.58 while native object bob/rotation and clip meanings/timing retained. No registered root travel. Every clip genuinely changes evaluated bone and armature-relative mesh coordinates. Gross actor scale/root/socket metadata remain fixed.\n\nReproduction in a separate writable copy of this object folder: run background /opt/homebrew/bin/blender --python source/build_round01.py; open the resulting source/round-01.blend with --python source/capture_round01.py; run source/publish_round01.py with the recorded Python/Pillow runtime; DEBUG=pw:browser node source/browser_round01.mjs; run source/browser_media_round01.py, source/audit_saved_round01.py in Blender, then source/finalize_round01.py. Preserve the reviewed folder immutable. Actual used source inputs/instructions/current099/570 helpers and React module snapshots are private under source/round-01-resources; runtime installations are recorded prerequisites, not vendored application trees.\n\nBrowser evidence: two Chromium153 actual launch modes, phone393x852/DPR1 atzoom0.4 and wide1840x640/DPR1 atlogical scale; all11states/all4facings for2.3seconds each. Actual RAF trace proves phase sequence, two loop wraps and terminal holds. Every frame of44 actual compositor videos is decoded, hash-bound and shown in labeled overview sheets; no APNG default-frame or sparse-video proxy is used. Original fullviewport webm files remain available. Complete native logical/phone phase sheets, current-helper sheets, light/gray/dark normal/contact-extreme screenshots and exact root/socket overlays are retained. Native/Pillow/CSS and mode raster residuals are measured rather than repaired.\n\nThe first development source save dropped unreferenced actions; its preserved failure log and source versions document the correction to fake-user retention before final capture. No final source or frame was altered after capture. No extra agents, target regeneration, original/preparation/brief/criteria/review mutation, packet creation, selfapproval, Git/production/deploy/live-Blender/device work. ROOT seals and the original independent judge reviews.\n'''
